-- Q4406: Nature and Scope of Engagements [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 200, the overall objective of the auditor is to obtain reasonable assurance about whether the financial statements as a whole are free from material misstatement, whether due to fraud or error, and to report on the findings. Reasonable assurance is a high but not absolute level of assurance.
Wrong (B): An audit does not guarantee freedom from all errors; reasonable assurance acknowledges inherent limitations.
Wrong (C): While fraud detection is considered, the audit objective is not to detect all fraud instances.
Wrong (D): Absolute assurance is unattainable due to inherent limitations of the audit process.$EXPL$
