-- Q4407: Nature and Scope of Engagements [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 315, the completeness assertion addresses whether all transactions, events, and account balances that should have been recorded have in fact been recorded. It is concerned with potential understatement of amounts in the financial statements.
Wrong (A): Existence addresses whether assets, liabilities, and equity interests actually exist at a given date—the opposite direction from completeness.
Wrong (C): Valuation addresses whether items are recorded at appropriate amounts, not whether all items are recorded.
Wrong (D): Rights and obligations addresses whether the entity holds rights to assets and owes liabilities, not recording completeness.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4407;

