  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): The existence assertion under AU-C 315 addresses whether assets, liabilities, and equity interests exist at a given date. By selecting items from the perpetual listing and physically locating them on the shelves, the auditor tests whether recorded inventory actually exists.
Wrong (A): Completeness would be tested by tracing from physical items to the records, not from records to physical items.
Wrong (B): Valuation and allocation addresses whether items are recorded at appropriate amounts, not physical presence.
