-- Q4409: Nature and Scope of Engagements [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): AU-C 200 defines reasonable assurance as a high, but not absolute, level of assurance. It is obtained when the auditor has gathered sufficient appropriate audit evidence to reduce audit risk to an acceptably low level. Inherent limitations prevent absolute assurance.
Wrong (A): A guarantee of detection is not achievable; reasonable assurance is not a guarantee.
Wrong (B): A moderate level of assurance describes limited assurance in a review engagement, not reasonable assurance.
Wrong (C): Absolute assurance is unattainable due to the inherent limitations of an audit.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4409;

